# DECISIONS.md 25 step 3's residue, frozen as a fixture: a `.env` carrying a
# variable NOTHING references, because the `.env` rename landed and the compose
# rename did not. It is inert by design and it CONVERGES — re-running the move
# finds the name already set to exactly the value being moved, treats that as a
# no-op, and writes the compose half.
#
# Story 9.6 is the reason this is a file rather than a paragraph: a staleness
# check that cannot tell this state from "somebody else set this name" turns
# the designed-inert residue into a hard refusal on the very re-run that was
# supposed to fix it.
COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=demo

POSTGRES_PASSWORD=hunter2
